PLAN=plan(6,'Patterns, expressions and equations','Part III · Patterns and symbols',16,'Scientific and technical innovation','Pattern, Equivalence','A pattern can be described by a rule; expressions, equations and formulas make the relationship precise and allow prediction and design.','How can a gardener order exactly the right number of border slabs for a square pond of any whole-number side length?','In order for a student to transfer mathematical knowledge, students must move between a diagram, a table, a rule and an equation, then check the result in context.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[3]['diagram']],['Describe and generalise a growing pattern.','Substitute into expressions and simplify or expand.','Solve linear equations and check solutions.','Use formulas and budget constraints in a design.'],'sequence · term · position · variable · expression · coefficient · like terms · expand · factorise · equation · formula · solution',sourcepages='114–132; answers 227–229')
